      "summaries": {
        "en": "CPython is the reference implementation of Python, providing the core interpreter that executes Python code and defines the language's standard behavior. Its key technical insight lies in the bytecode compilation model—Python source code is first compiled to platform-independent bytecode, which is then executed by the CPython virtual machine, balancing portability with performance. Developers can use CPython to run any Python application, extend it with C modules for performance-critical tasks, or study its source code to understand language implementation details and contribute to Python's evolution.",
        "zh": "CPython是Python语言的参考实现，作为核心解释器执行Python代码并定义语言标准行为。其关键技术在于字节码编译模型：Python源代码先被编译为平台无关的字节码，再由CPython虚拟机执行，在可移植性与性能间取得平衡。开发者可通过CPython运行各类Python应用，用C扩展模块优化性能关键任务，或研究其源码理解语言实现机制，参与Python生态演进。这个开源项目展示了如何通过清晰的架构设计支撑动态语言的灵活性与效率，适合作为学习编译器原理和参与开源贡献的实践平台。",
        "es": "CPython is the reference implementation of Python, providing the core interpreter that executes Python code and defines the language's standard behavior. Its key technical insight lies in the bytecode compilation model—Python source code is first compiled to platform-independent bytecode, which is then executed by the CPython virtual machine, balancing portability with performance. Developers can use CPython to run any Python application, extend it with C modules for performance-critical tasks, or study its source code to understand language implementation details and contribute to Python's evolution.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "cpython gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "CPython is the reference implementation of Python, providing the core interpreter that executes Python code and defines the language's standard behavior. Its key technical insight lies in the bytecode compilation model—Python source code is first compiled to platform-independent bytecode, which is then executed by the CPython virtual machine, balancing portability with performance. Developers can use CPython to run any Python application, extend it with C modules for performance-critical tasks, or study its source code to understand language implementation details and contribute to Python's evolution.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/python/cpython for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
